-## 🆕 What's new in 1.6.0 / Nouveautés de la 1.6.0
+## 🆕 What's new in 1.6.1 / Nouveautés de la 1.6.1
 
-The Kanban becomes an agile board: Failed and Abandoned columns, sprints, swimlanes, list and timeline views, reports, labels and quick filters, cards coloured by type, quick add, right-click menus and multi-select, and a board you can ask questions in any language. Each AI provider and each forge takes several accounts (a default, a monthly budget, one pinned per project or card, failover to the same provider's other accounts first); OpenRouter, Hugging Face and Bitbucket Cloud join the list. The app now decides where a task's long test suites run (here, on the forge's CI or on the server), pull requests get approval tiers N0 to N3, code mode lets agents run one script instead of many calls, and a task can run in its own microVM. The team server measures usage within the GDPR, sends a daily report and enforces monthly token budgets, and the mobile app is redesigned. → [Roadmap](Roadmap) · [Feuille de route](Roadmap.fr) · [Release notes](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/releases)
+A sprint's **Plan** view shows its capacity against the velocity of the last sprints and moves tasks by drag and drop or the keyboard, with undo, quick backlog filters and « Estimate ». **Propose the sprint** fills it up to its capacity: rules rank the backlog and add what a task waits on first, the selected provider's model picks among the best and gives a reason per task (rules alone without a model), with variants, a suggested goal and one undoable « Add N tasks ». Dates, times and date pickers now follow the app's language on the desktop and the phone, a task's microVM stays closed to its allowlist, and the release builds run on a Node.js REA accepts. → [Roadmap](Roadmap) · [Feuille de route](Roadmap.fr) · [Release notes](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/releases)
 
-Un Kanban agile qu'on interroge, plusieurs comptes par IA et par forge, et des suites longues placées là où elles tiennent.
+Planifier et proposer un sprint avec l'IA, et des dates dans la langue de l'app.
+
+Before that, **1.6.0** made the Kanban an agile board you can ask questions, with several accounts per AI provider and per forge: see the [Roadmap](Roadmap).
 
